From: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
Date: 2026-05-11
Subject: [PATCH] C-04: normalize GpuGlyphKey font_size for distance-field reps (FIXING.md)
Risk: Medium — requires build + tests (glyph identity). Do NOT apply without CI.
Refs: FIXING.md C-04 (include/chronon3d/runtime/gpu_glyph_atlas.hpp:34)

Problem:
  GpuGlyphKey::operator== and GpuGlyphKeyHash ignore font_size for
  Mtsdf/Msdf/Sdf, but callers may still construct keys with varying
  font_size. Two logically distinct DistanceFieldProfile glyphs collapse
  to the same key → wrong distance_range_px in shader. SSOT violation.

Fix:
  Provide a factory that normalizes font_size to 0 for distance-field
  representations at construction time. Callers should use it instead
  of aggregate initialization. Existing hash/equality stays compatible
  (they already ignore the field); this prevents accidental divergence
  at the call site.

diff --git a/include/chronon3d/runtime/gpu_glyph_atlas.hpp b/include/chronon3d/runtime/gpu_glyph_atlas.hpp
--- a/include/chronon3d/runtime/gpu_glyph_atlas.hpp
+++ b/include/chronon3d/runtime/gpu_glyph_atlas.hpp
@@ -30,6 +30,23 @@
 struct GpuGlyphKey {
     std::string font_path;
     std::uint32_t glyph_id{0};
     std::uint64_t variation_hash{0};
     GlyphRepresentation representation{GlyphRepresentation::Mtsdf};
     std::uint16_t generation_profile{0};
     std::uint32_t font_size{0};
+
+    // FIXING.md C-04 — canonical factory. For distance-field reps
+    // (Mtsdf/Msdf/Sdf) the runtime font size is a layout concern and
+    // must not participate in identity. Normalize to 0 so that equality
+    // and hashing are SSOT-consistent even when callers pass a stale
+    // font_size.
+    [[nodiscard]] static GpuGlyphKey make(std::string font_path,
+                                          std::uint32_t glyph_id,
+                                          std::uint64_t variation_hash,
+                                          GlyphRepresentation rep,
+                                          std::uint16_t generation_profile,
+                                          std::uint32_t font_size) noexcept {
+        if (rep != GlyphRepresentation::Coverage) font_size = 0;
+        return GpuGlyphKey{std::move(font_path), glyph_id, variation_hash,
+                           rep, generation_profile, font_size};
+    }
 
     /// Runtime font size is a layout concern for distance fields.  It is part
     /// of identity only for Coverage, whose pixels are raster-size-specific.
